celld patch 0003: dolt_checkout --carry-ignored.

Why. A Dolt working set is per branch, so a table that is not versioned
(a table that dolt_ignore covers and no commit holds) exists once for each
branch that was ever checked out, and a checkout leaves the new branch with
a stale copy or none. celld keeps its own runtime tables (_cf_KV, the alarm
and wake records, ...) and a class's declared local tables in such tables,
and they must follow the cell wherever it is checked out. Without this patch
celld copied them row by row on every checkout, so a checkout cost as much
as the local state is large.

What. dolt_checkout accepts --carry-ignored. The session's untracked ignored
tables (the same set the merge and pull paths carry across a moving branch:
mergeFindLocalTables, mergeCopyLocalTables) are grafted onto the target
branch's working catalog by catalog entry, so a table of the same name that
the target held from an earlier visit is replaced and no row is read or
written. The branch being left keeps its own copy, which is stale from then
on. A table the target commit holds under the same name with different
content is not carried. Without the flag nothing changes.

